{"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLTextElementData\/dir"},"metadata":{"roleHeading":"Instance Property","title":"dir","symbolKind":"property","externalID":"s:7IvorMXL18MXLTextElementDataV3dirAA0C9DirectionOvp","modules":[{"name":"IvorMXL"}],"fragments":[{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"dir","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLTextDirection","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL16MXLTextDirectionO","kind":"typeIdentifier"}],"role":"symbol"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLTextElementData"]]},"sections":[],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"patch":0,"minor":3},"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The text-direction attribute is used to adjust and override the Unicode bidirectional text algorithm, similar"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"to the Directionality data category in the W3C Internationalization Tag Set recommendation."}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"platforms":["macOS"],"tokens":[{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"dir","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLTextDirection","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLTextDirection","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL16MXLTextDirectionO","kind":"typeIdentifier"}],"languages":["swift"]}]},{"content":[{"level":2,"text":"Discussion","anchor":"discussion","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Maps to the MusicXML "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"dir"},{"type":"text","text":" attribute."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxltextelementdata\/dir"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"references":{"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLTextElementData":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLTextElementData","title":"MXLTextElementData","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLTextElementData"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MXLTextElementData","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxltextelementdata","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The text-element-data type represents a syllable or portion of a syllable for lyric text underlay. A hyphen in"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the string content should only be used for an actual hyphenated word. Language names for text elements come","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"from ISO 639, with optional country subcodes from ISO 3166.","type":"text"}]},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLTextDirection":{"kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MXLTextDirection","kind":"identifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxltextdirection","title":"MXLTextDirection","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"enum","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLTextDirection","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLTextDirection","abstract":[{"text":"The text-direction type is used to adjust and override the Unicode bidirectional text algorithm, similar to","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the Directionality data category in the W3C Internationalization Tag Set recommendation. Values are ltr (left-","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"to-right embed), rtl (right-to-left embed), lro (left-to-right bidi-override), and rlo (right-to-left bidi-","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"override). The default value is ltr. This type is typically used by applications that store text in left-to-","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"right visual order rather than logical order. Such applications can use the lro value to better communicate","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"with other applications that more fully support bidirectional text.","type":"text"}]},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A MusicXML parser, normalizer, validator, and formatter."}],"title":"IvorMXL","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl","type":"topic","role":"collection"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLTextElementData/dir":{"title":"dir","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"text":"dir","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLTextDirection","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL16MXLTextDirectionO","kind":"typeIdentifier"}],"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxltextelementdata\/dir","abstract":[{"text":"The text-direction attribute is used to adjust and override the Unicode bidirectional text algorithm, similar","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"to the Directionality data category in the W3C Internationalization Tag Set recommendation.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLTextElementData\/dir"}}}